(2521, 'Alb', 'A vestment of white linen reaching to the feet an enveloping the person    in the Roman Catholic church worn by those in holy orders when officiating at mass It was formerly worn at least by clerics in daily life'),
(2522, 'Albacore', 'A name applied to several large fishes of the Mackerel family Scombridae esp Thunnus alalunga formerly Orcynus alalonga it is a type of tuna or tunny  The name has been also applied to a larger related species Thunnus thynnus formerly Orcynus thynnus common in the Mediterranean and Atlantic which is called in New England the horse mackerel'),
