(2526, 'Albatross', 'A web footed bird of the genus Diomedea of which there are several species They are the largest of sea birds capable of long continued flight and are often seen at great distances from the land They are found chiefly in the southern hemisphere'),
(2527, 'Albe', 'Although albeit'),
