(3642, 'Amp', 'The unit of electric current    defined by the International Electrical Congress in 1893 and by U S Statute as one tenth of the unit of current of the C G S system of electro magnetic units or the practical equivalent of the unvarying current which when passed through a standard solution of nitrate of silver in water deposits silver at the rate of 0001118 grams per second Called also the international amp'),
