(3937, 'anaphylactic shock', 'Shock resulting from anaphylaxis2  It is a severe form of physiological shock often having a fatal outcome and is caused by an extreme immunological reaction to antigens  It is characterized by smooth muscle contraction and capillary dilation throughout the body initiated by antibodies of the IgE class  It is usually seen when an antigen to which a person has become hypersensitized is injected intravenously or subcutaneously  It is also called generalyzed anaphylaxis or systemic anaphylaxis and sometimes anaphylaxis'),
