(8903, 'Bask', 'To lie in warmth to be exposed to genial heat'),
(8904, 'Basket', 'A vessel made of osiers or other twigs cane rushes splints or other flexible material interwoven'),
(8905, 'Basketball', 'A ball game usually played indoors in an area called the basketball court in which two opposing teams of five players each contest with each other to toss a large inflated ball the basketball into opposite goals baskets resembling baskets each typically a cylindrical mesh suspended from a circular rim which is held ten feet above the court  A goal scored by passing the basketball through the basket may count from one to three points depending on the situation in which it was thrown'),
