(13800, 'Cabas', 'A flat basket or frail for figs etc hence a ladys flat workbasket reticule or hand bag    often written caba'),
(13801, 'Cabassou', 'A species of armadillo of the genus Xenurus Xenurus unicinctus and Xenurus hispidus the tatouay'),
(13802, 'Cabbage', 'An esculent vegetable of many varieties derived from the wild Brassica oleracea of Europe  The common cabbage has a compact head of leaves  The cauliflower Brussels sprouts etc are sometimes classed as cabbages'),
(13803, 'cabbage butterfly', 'a white butterfly Pieris rap'),
