(13970, 'Cahoot', 'Partnership league as to go in cahoot or in cahoots with a person  Usually used in the plural and in modern usage often used to imply that the joint effort is unethical shady questionable or illegal as a shill in cahoots with a pickpocket to serve as a distraction'),
