(16115, 'Ceremony', 'Ar act or series of acts often of a symbolical character prescribed by law custom or authority in the conduct of important matters as in the performance of religious duties the transaction of affairs of state and the celebration of notable events as the ceremony of crowning a sovereign the ceremonies observed in consecrating a church marriage and baptismal ceremonies'),
