(16129, 'Cerium', 'A rare metallic element occurring in the minerals cerite allanite monazite etc  Symbol Ce  Atomic weight 1415 It resembles iron in color and luster but is soft and both malleable and ductile It tarnishes readily in the air'),
(16130, 'Cernuous', 'Inclining or nodding downward pendulous drooping    said of a bud flower fruit or the capsule of a moss'),
(16131, 'Cero', 'A large and valuable fish of the Mackerel family of the genus Scomberomorus  Two species are found in the West Indies and less commonly on the Atlantic coast of the United States    the common cero Scomberomorus caballa called also kingfish and spotted or king cero Scomberomorus regalis'),
(16132, 'Cerograph', 'A writing on wax'),
(16133, 'Cerographic', 'Of or pertaining to cerography'),
(16134, 'Cerographist', 'One who practices cerography'),
(16135, 'Cerolite', 'A hydrous silicate of magnesium allied to serpentine occurring in waxlike masses of a yellow or greenish color'),
(16136, 'Ceroma', 'The unguent a composition of oil and wax with which wrestlers were anointed among the ancient Romans'),
(16137, 'Ceromancy', 'Divination by dropping melted wax in water'),
(16138, 'Ceroon', 'A bale or package covered with hide or with wood bound with hide as a ceroon of indigo cochineal etc'),
(16139, 'Ceroplastic', 'Relating to the art of modeling in wax'),
(16140, 'Ceroplastics', 'The art of modeling in wax'),
(16141, 'Cerosin', 'A waxy substance obtained from the bark of the sugar cane and crystallizing in delicate white lamin'),
