(33516, 'Erysipelothrix', 'a genus of non motile rod shaped Gram positive bacteria of the family Corynebacteriaceae  They are facultatively anaerobic and produce acid but no gas from glucose  Members of this genus are parasitic on fish birds and mammals including man  The type species of the genus Erysipelothrix rhusiopathiae causes erysipeloid in man'),
