(37569, 'Flying fox', 'a fruit bat of the genus Pteropus which has a head resembling that of a fox'),
(37570, 'Flying lemur', 'either of two nocturnal lemurlike mammals inhabiting the East Indies Cynocephalus variegatus or the Phillipines Cynocephalus volans having broad folds of skin between the fore and hind limbs on both sides of the body allowing them to make long gliding leaps they have been classed in the separate order Dermoptera  They are arboreal and have become rare'),
(37571, 'Flying squirrel', 'One of a group of squirrels of the genus Glaucomys formerly Pteromus and Sciuropterus 1913 Webster especially Glaucomys volans and Glaucomys sabrinus having parachute like folds of skin extending from the fore to the hind legs which enable them to make very long gliding leaps'),
