(39200, 'Funeral', 'The solemn rites used in the disposition of a dead human body whether such disposition be by interment burning or otherwise esp the ceremony or solemnization of interment obsequies burial    formerly used in the plural'),
(39201, 'funeral home', 'An establishment usually commercial where the bodies of dead persons are prepared for viewing before burial or cremation called also funeral parlor mortuary funeral chapel and informally undertakers  The body may or may not be preserved by embalming before viewing or burial and in some cases the body is not exposed for viewing though present in a casket  Often some form of memorial service is held for the deceased at the funeral home where friends and relatives may come to pay their respects to the dead and express condolence to the family  The work of preparation of the body and many other arrangements related to the funeral and burial are carried out by an undertaker or mortician who manages the funeral home'),
