(42376, 'Guidon', 'A small flag or streamer as that carried by cavalry which is broad at one end and nearly pointed at the other or that used to direct the movements of a body of infantry or to make signals at sea also the flag of a guild or fraternity In the United States service each company of cavalry has a guidon'),
