(42403, 'Guinea pig', 'A small Brazilian rodent Cavia porcellus or Cavia cobaya about seven inches in length and usually of a white color with spots of orange and black  Called also cavy  It is the domesticated form of the wild cavy often kept as a pet and used commonly as an experimental animal in laboratory research'),
