(43599, 'Hawk', 'One of numerous species and genera of rapacious birds of the family Falconidae  They differ from the true falcons in lacking the prominent tooth and notch of the bill and in having shorter and less pointed wings  Many are of large size and grade into the eagles Some as the goshawk were formerly trained like falcons  In a more general sense the word is not infrequently applied also to true falcons as the sparrow hawk pigeon hawk duck hawk and prairie hawk'),
