(44213, 'Hemophilia', 'A condition characterized by a tendency to profuse and uncontrollable hemorrhage from the slightest wounds it is caused by an absence or abnormality of a clotting factor in the blood and is a recessive genetic disease linked to the X chromosome and therefore usually occurs only in males there are several specific forms  It may be treated by administering purified clotting factor  It was formerly termed Hematophilia'),
