(44434, 'Hermaphrodeity', 'Hermaphrodism'),
(44435, 'Hermaphrodism', 'See Hermaphroditism'),
(44436, 'Hermaphrodite', 'An individual which has the attributes of both male and female or which unites in itself the two sexes an animal or plant having the parts of generation of both sexes as when a flower contains both the stamens and pistil within the same calyx or on the same receptacle In some cases reproduction may take place without the union of the distinct individuals In the animal kingdom true hermaphrodites are found only among the invertebrates See Illust in Appendix under Helminths'),
(44437, 'Hermaphroditic', 'Partaking of the characteristics of both sexes having male and female reproductive organs in the same plant or animal characterized by hermaphroditism  Opposite of dioecious'),
(44438, 'Hermaphroditism', 'The union of the two sexes in the same individual or the combination of some of their characteristics or organs in one individual'),
(44439, 'Hermeneutic', 'Unfolding the signification of or pertaining to interpretation exegetical explanatory as hermeneutic theology or the art of expounding the Scriptures a hermeneutic phrase'),
(44440, 'Hermeneutically', 'According to the principles of interpretation as a verse of Scripture was examined hermeneutically'),
