(44506, 'Hertz', 'a unit of frequency equal to one cycle per second it is abbreviated Hz  It is commonly used to specify the frequency of radio waves and also the clock frequencies in digital computers  For these applications kilohertz and megahertz are the most commonly used units derived from hertz'),
