(44556, 'Heterodont', 'Having the teeth differentiated into incisors canines and molars as in man    opposed to homodont'),
(44557, 'Heterodox', 'Contrary to or differing from some acknowledged standard as the Bible the creed of a church the decree of a council and the like not orthodox heretical    said of opinions doctrines books etc esp upon theological subjects'),
