(44934, 'hinterland', 'a remote and undeveloped area originally the land or region lying behind the coast district The term is used esp with reference to the so called doctrine of the hinterland sometimes advanced that occupation of the coast supports a claim to an exclusive right to occupy from time to time the territory lying inland of the coast'),
(44935, 'Hintingly', 'In a hinting manner'),
(44936, 'Hip', 'To dislocate or sprain the hip of to fracture or injure the hip bone of a quadruped in such a manner as to produce a permanent depression of that side'),
(44937, 'hipbone', 'Either of two large flaring bones each forming one half of the pelvis made up of the ilium and ischium and pubis'),
(44938, 'Hipe', 'A throw in which the wrestler lifts his opponent from the ground swings him to one side knocks up his nearer thigh from the back with the knee and throws him on his back'),
(44939, 'hipflask', 'A small portable flask usually made of metal used to hold liquor'),
(44940, 'Hiphalt', 'Lame in the hip'),
(44941, 'hipless', 'having hips which are not prominent seeming to have no hips as slim and hipless    of people  Opposite of broad hipped'),
(44942, 'hipline', 'the line formed by measuring the hip at its greatest part'),
(44943, 'Hip lock', 'A lock in which a close grip is obtained and a fall attempted by a heave over the hip'),
(44944, 'Hippa', 'A genus of marine decapod crustaceans which burrow rapidly in the sand by pushing themselves backward    called also bait bug See Illust under Anomura'),
(44945, 'Hipparion', 'An extinct genus of Tertiary mammals allied to the horse but three toed having on each foot a small lateral hoof on each side of the main central one It is believed to be one of the ancestral genera of the Horse family'),
(44946, 'hippeastrum', 'An amaryllis of tropical America Hippeastrum puniceum often cultivated as a houseplant for its showy white to red flowers'),
(44947, 'Hipped', 'Somewhat hypochondriac melancholy See Hyppish'),
(44948, 'hippie', 'Someone who rejects the established culture dresses casually and advocates extreme liberalism in politics and lifestyle  Used especially of those in the late 1960s mostly in their late teens and early twenties who conspicuously rejected traditional culture by dressing casually if male wore their hair long and wore folksy or used clothing adorned with beads headbands and often flowers they emphasized the importance of love and direct personal relations rather than success oriented businesslike behavior strove for spontaneity sometimes lived communally and in some cases tried to expand their consciousness by various psychological techniques such as meditation or through the use of consciousness altering drugs such as marijuana or LSD  By the end of the Vietnam war in the 1970s the numbers of people living a visibly hippie lifestyle had dramatically decreased though some people continue to develop similar views and live with the same outlook'),
(44949, 'hippo', 'Same as hippopotamus'),
(44950, 'Hippobosca', 'A genus of dipterous insects including the horsefly or horse tick'),
(44951, 'Hippoboscidae', 'A natural family of winged or wingless dipterans louse flies'),
(44952, 'Hippocamp', 'See Hippocampus'),
(44953, 'Hippocampal', 'Of or pertaining to the hippocampus'),
(44954, 'Hippocampus', 'A fabulous monster with the head and fore quarters of a horse joined to the tail of a dolphin or other fish Hippocampus brevirostris    seen in Pompeian paintings attached to the chariot of Neptune'),
(44955, 'Hippocentaur', 'Same as Centaur'),
(44956, 'Hippocras', 'A cordial made of spiced wine etc'),
(44957, 'Hippocrates', 'A famous Greek physician and medical writer born in Cos about 460 b c'),
(44958, 'Hippocratic', 'Of or pertaining to Hippocrates or to his teachings'),
(44959, 'Hippocratic oath', 'An oath said to have been dictated by Hippocrates to his disciples  Such an oath is still administered to candidates for graduation in medicine'),
(44960, 'Hippocratism', 'The medical philosophy or system of Hippocrates'),
(44961, 'Hippocrene', 'A fountain on Mount Helicon in B'),
(44962, 'Hippocrepian', 'One of an order of fresh water Bryozoa in which the tentacles are on a lophophore shaped like a horseshoe See Phylactol'),
(44963, 'Hippocrepiform', 'Shaped like a horseshoe'),
(44964, 'Hippodame', 'A fabulous sea monster'),
