(44974, 'Hippophile', 'One who loves horses'),
(44975, 'Hippopotamus', 'A large amphibious herbivorous mammal Hippopotamus amphibius common in the rivers of tropical Africa It is allied to the hogs and has a very thick naked skin a thick and square head a very large muzzle small eyes and ears thick and heavy body and short legs It is supposed to be the behemoth of the Bible Called also zeekoe and river horse  A smaller species Hippopotamus Liberiencis inhabits Western Africa'),
(44976, 'Hippotomy', 'Anatomy of the horse'),
(44977, 'Hippuric', 'Obtained from the urine of horses as hippuric acid'),
(44978, 'Hippurite', 'A fossil bivalve mollusk of the genus Hippurites of many species having a conical cup shaped under valve with a flattish upper valve or lid Hippurites are found only in the Cretaceous rocks'),
(44979, 'Hip roofed', 'Having a hip roof'),
(44980, 'Hipshot', 'Having the hip dislocated hence having one hip lower than the other'),
(44981, 'hipster', 'A person who is hip2 a'),
(44982, 'Hip tree', 'The dog rose'),
(44983, 'Hir', 'See Here pron'),
(44984, 'Hircic', 'Of pertaining to or derived from mutton suet    applied by Chevreul to an oily acid which was obtained from mutton suet and to which he attributed the peculiar taste and smell of that substance The substance has also been called hircin'),
(44985, 'Hircin', 'Hircic acid See Hircic'),
(44986, 'Hircine', 'Goatlike of or pertaining to a goat or the goats'),
(44987, 'Hire', 'See Here pron'),
(44988, 'hired', 'performing work for pay as hired hands'),
(44989, 'Hireless', 'Without hire'),
(44990, 'Hireling', 'One who is hired or who serves for wages esp one whose motive and interest in serving another are wholly gainful a mercenary'),
(44991, 'Hire purchase', 'A contract more fully called contract of hire with an option of purchase in which a person hires goods for a specified period and at a fixed rent with the added condition that if he shall retain the goods for the full period and pay all the installments of rent as they become due the contract shall determine and the title vest absolutely in him and that if he chooses he may at any time during the term surrender the goods and be quit of any liability for future installments upon the contract In the United States such a contract is generally treated as a conditional sale and the term hire purchase is also sometimes applied to a contract in which the hirer is not free to avoid future liability by surrender of the goods In England however if the hirer does not have this right the contract is a sale'),
(44992, 'Hirer', 'One who hires'),
(44993, 'Hires', 'Hers theirs See Here pron'),
(44994, 'Hirsute', 'Rough with hair set with bristles shaggy'),
(44995, 'Hirsuteness', 'Hairiness'),
(44996, 'Hirtellous', 'Pubescent with minute and somewhat rigid hairs'),
