(52916, 'Kitcat', 'Designating a club in London to which Addison and Steele belonged    so called from Christopher Cat a pastry cook who served the club with mutton pies'),
(52917, 'Kitchen', 'A room equipped for cooking food the room of a house restaurant or other building appropriated to cookery'),
