(54319, 'Lazuli', 'A mineral of a fine azure blue color usually in small rounded masses It is essentially a silicate of alumina lime and soda with some sodium sulphide is often marked by yellow spots or veins of sulphide of iron and is much valued for ornamental work  Called also lapis lazuli and Armenian stone'),
