(54835, 'Letts', 'An Indo European people allied to the Lithuanians and Old Prussians and inhabiting a part of the Baltic provinces of Russia'),
(54836, 'Lettuce', 'A composite plant of the genus Lactuca Lactuca sativa the leaves of which are used as salad  Plants of this genus yield a milky juice from which lactucarium is obtained  The commonest wild lettuce of the United States is Lactuca Canadensis'),
