(55445, 'Link motion', 'A valve gear consisting of two eccentrics with their rods giving motion to a slide valve by an adjustable connecting bar called the link in such a way that the motion of the engine can be reversed or the cut off varied at will    used very generally in locomotives and marine engines'),
