(55456, 'Linotype', 'A kind of typesetting machine which produces castings each of which corresponds to a line of separate types By pressing the keys of a keyboard like one on a typewriter the matrices for one line are properly arranged the entire line or stereotype or slug is then cast and planed and the matrices are returned to their proper places the whole process being automatic'),
