(55486, 'Lions tail', 'A genus of labiate plants Leonurus    so called from a fancied resemblance of its flower spikes to the tuft of a lions tail Leonurus Cardiaca is the common motherwort'),
(55487, 'Lions tooth', 'See Leontodon'),
(55488, 'Lip', 'One of the two fleshy folds which surround the orifice of the mouth in man and many other animals In man the lips are organs of speech essential to certain articulations Hence by a figure they denote the mouth or all the organs of speech and sometimes speech itself'),
(55489, 'Lipans', 'A tribe of North American Indians inhabiting the northern part of Mexico They belong to the Tinneh stock and are closely related to the Apaches'),
