(55493, 'Liparite', 'A quartzose trachyte rhyolite'),
(55494, 'lipemia', 'The presence of an abnormally high concentration of lipid in the blood  Called also hyperlipemia hyperlipidemia hyperlipoidemia lipidemia lipoidemia'),
(55495, 'lipfern', 'any of various terrestrial ferns of the genus Cheilanthes they are cosmopolitan in arid and semi arid temperate or tropical regions'),
(55496, 'Lipic', 'Pertaining to or derived from fat The word was formerly used specifically to designate a supposed acid obtained by the oxidation of oleic acid tallow wax etc'),
(55497, 'lipid', 'Any of a variety of oily or greasy organic compounds found as major structural components of living cells they are insoluble in water but soluble in organic solvents such as alcohol and ether and include the common fats cholesterol and other steroids phospholipids sphingolipids waxes and fatty acids some of the lipids together with proteins and carbohydrates form an essential structural component of living cells as in the cell walls and membranes  The term lipid refers to its solubility in nonpolar solvents and has no significance with regard to chemical structure'),
(55498, 'lipide', 'Same as lipid'),
(55499, 'lipidemia', 'Same as lipemia'),
(55500, 'lipid lowering', 'Serving to reduce the concentration of lipid such as cholesterol in the blood    of medications such as Mevinolin that are used especially to reduce blood cholesterol as a preventive measure against heart disease'),
(55501, 'lipidosis', 'A disorder of lipid metabolism whether congenital or acquired'),
