(55640, 'lithoglyptics', 'The art of cutting and engraving gems'),
(55641, 'lithograph', 'To trace on stone by the process of lithography so as to transfer the design to paper by printing as to lithograph a design to lithograph a painting See lithography'),
(55642, 'lithographer', 'One who lithographs one who practices lithography'),
(55643, 'lithographic', 'Of or pertaining to lithography made by lithography as the lithographic art a lithographic picture'),
(55644, 'Lithography', 'The art or process of putting designs or writing with a greasy material on stone and of producing printed impressions therefrom The process depends in the main upon the antipathy between grease and water which prevents a printing ink containing oil from adhering to wetted parts of the stone not covered by the design See Lithographic limestone under Lithographic'),
