(55851, 'Lobelin', 'A yellowish green resin from Lobelia used as an emetic and diaphoretic'),
(55852, 'Lobeline', 'A poisonous narcotic alkaloid extracted from the leaves of Indian tobacco Lobelia inflata as a yellow oil having a tobaccolike taste and odor'),
(55853, 'Lobiped', 'Having lobate toes as a coot'),
(55854, 'Loblolly', 'Gruel porridge    so called among seamen'),
(55855, 'Lobosa', 'An order of Rhizopoda in which the pseudopodia are thick and irregular in form as in the Am'),
(55856, 'Lobotes', 'The type genus of the Lobotidae'),
