(56169, 'Look', 'To direct the eyes for the purpose of seeing something to direct the eyes toward an object to observe with the eyes while keeping them directed    with various prepositions often in a special or figurative sense See Phrases below'),
(56170, 'lookdown', 'A fish Selene vomer similar to the moonfish but with eyes high on the truncated forehead it was also called moonfish at one time'),
