(56936, 'Machinal', 'Of or pertaining to machines'),
(56937, 'Machinate', 'To plan to contrive esp to form a scheme with the purpose of doing harm to contrive artfully to plot'),
(56938, 'Machination', 'The act of machinating'),
(56939, 'Machinator', 'One who machinates or forms a scheme with evil designs a plotter or artful schemer'),
(56940, 'Machine', 'In general any combination of bodies so connected that their relative motions are constrained and by means of which force and motion may be transmitted and modified as a screw and its nut or a lever arranged to turn about a fulcrum or a pulley about its pivot etc especially a construction more or less complex consisting of a combination of moving parts or simple mechanical elements as wheels levers cams etc with their supports and connecting framework calculated to constitute a prime mover or to receive force and motion from a prime mover or from another machine and transmit modify and apply them to the production of some desired mechanical effect or work as weaving by a loom or the excitation of electricity by an electrical machine'),
(56941, 'machine bolt', 'A threaded hexagonal or square headed bolt with a nut it is tightened with a wrench and used to connect metal parts'),
(56942, 'machine code', 'Same as machine language'),
(56943, 'machine controlled', 'same as automated'),
(56944, 'machine gun', 'A fully automatic rapid firing rifle which continues to fire bullets repeatedly as long as the trigger is depressed lighter versions may be carried in the hands and heavier versions may be mounted on a tripod vehicle or other mount  The lighweight versions are sometimes called a submachine gun'),
(56945, 'machine gunner', 'A soldier who operates a machine gun'),
(56946, 'machine language', 'a set of instructions3 in a binary form that can be executed directly by the CPU of a computer without translation by a computer program'),
(56947, 'machinelike', 'behaving in an unthinking manner like the functioning of a machine as machine like fools'),
