(57366, 'maidenhair', 'Any of various small to large terrestrial ferns of the genus Adiantum having very slender graceful stalks and delicate palmately branched fronds especially  Adiantum pedatum  It is common in the United States and is sometimes used in medicine  The name is also applied to other species of the same genus as to the Venus hair'),
