(57453, 'Maintain', 'To hold or keep in any particular state or condition to support to sustain to uphold to keep up not to suffer to fail or decline as to maintain a certain degree of heat in a furnace to maintain a fence or a railroad to maintain the digestive process or powers of the stomach to maintain the fertility of soil to maintain present reputation'),
