(57977, 'Mango', 'The fruit of the mango tree It is rather larger than an apple and of an ovoid shape Some varieties are fleshy and luscious and others tough and tasting of turpentine The green fruit is pickled for market'),
(57978, 'mango tree', 'An East Indian tree of the genus Mangifera Mangifera Indica related to the cashew and the sumac  It grows to a large size and produces a large oval smooth skinned fruit which is the mango of commerce  It is now cultivated in tropical America'),
