(57984, 'Mangosteen', 'A tree of the East Indies of the genus Garcinia Garcinia Mangostana with thick leathery leaves  The tree grows to the height of eighteen feet and bears fruit also called mangosteen of the size of a small apple the pulp of which is very delicious food'),
(57985, 'Mangrove', 'The name of one or two trees of the genus Rhizophora Rhizophora Mangle and Rhizophora mucronata the last doubtfully distinct inhabiting muddy shores of tropical regions where they spread by emitting aerial roots which fasten in the saline mire and eventually become new stems The seeds also send down a strong root while yet attached to the parent plant'),
