(58360, 'Margosa', 'A large tree of the genus Melia Melia Azadirachta found in India  Its bark is bitter and used as a tonic  A valuable oil is expressed from its seeds and a tenacious gum exudes from its trunk  The Melia Azedarach is a much more showy tree and is cultivated in the Southern United States where it is known as Pride of India Pride of China or bead tree  Various parts of the tree are considered anthelmintic'),
