(58379, 'Marined', 'Having the lower part of the body like a fish'),
(58380, 'marine mine', 'A military explosive device designed to be placed on or under the surface of a body of water and to explode when ships pass nearby or come in contact with it  Its function is to destroy enemy ships or deny hostile naval forces access to certain areas of the sea usually near the shoreline  Also called underwater mine and floating mine and previously referred to as a torpedo See torpedo2 a'),
