(59195, 'Melain', 'The dark coloring matter of the liquid of the cuttlefish'),
(59196, 'Melainotype', 'See Melanotype'),
(59197, 'Melam', 'A white or buff colored granular powder C6H9N11 obtained by heating ammonium sulphocyanate'),
(59198, 'melamine', 'A nitrogenous strongly basic chemical substance C3H6N6 structurally 246 triamino 135 triazine produced from several cyanogen compounds and obtained as a white crystalline substance    formerly supposed to be produced by the decomposition of melam  Called also cyanuramide  It is used as one of the starting components together with formaldehyde in the preparation of melamine resins including the commercially marketed Formica TM  It is solid at room temperature and sublimes at temperatures approaching 250'),
(59199, 'melamine resin', 'A thermosetting plastic formed by the reaction of melamine and formaldehyde  It is used for molding and for preparing laminated sheets used to surface counter tops walls and furniture  The commercially marketed Formica TM is one type of melamine resin'),
(59200, 'Melampode', 'The black hellebore'),
(59201, 'Melampsoraceae', 'A natural family of rust fungi'),
(59202, 'Melampyrin', 'The saccharine substance dulcite    so called because found in the leaves of cowwheat Melampyrum See Dulcite'),
(59203, 'Melanaemia', 'A morbid condition in which the blood contains black pigment either floating freely or imbedded in the white blood corpuscles'),
(59204, 'Melanagogue', 'A medicine supposed to expel black bile or choler'),
(59205, 'Melancholia', 'A kind of mental unsoundness characterized by extreme depression of spirits ill grounded fears delusions and brooding over one particular subject or train of ideas'),
(59206, 'Melancholian', 'A person affected with melancholy a melancholic'),
(59207, 'Melancholic', 'Given to melancholy depressed melancholy dejected unhappy'),
(59208, 'Melancholily', 'In a melancholy manner'),
(59209, 'Melancholiness', 'The state or quality of being melancholy'),
(59210, 'Melancholious', 'Melancholy'),
(59211, 'Melancholist', 'One affected with melancholy or dejection'),
(59212, 'Melancholize', 'To become gloomy or dejected in mind'),
(59213, 'Melancholy', 'Depressed in spirits dejected gloomy dismal'),
(59214, 'Melanconiaceae', 'A family of fungi constituting the order Melanconiales'),
(59215, 'Melanconiales', 'The smallest of the three orders of Fungi Imperfecti including those with no asci nor pycnidia but as a rule having the spores in cavities without special walls  They cause many of the plant diseases known as anthracnose'),
(59216, 'Melanesian', 'Of or pertaining to Melanesia'),
(59217, 'Melanian', 'One of a family of fresh water pectinibranchiate mollusks having a turret shaped shell'),
(59218, 'Melanic', 'Melanotic'),
(59219, 'Melaniline', 'A complex nitrogenous hydrocarbon obtained artificially as by the action of cyanogen chloride on aniline as a white crystalline substance    called also diphenyl guanidin'),
(59220, 'Melanin', 'A black pigment found in the pigment bearing cells of the skin particularly in the skin of the negro in the epithelial cells of the external layer of the retina then called fuscin in the outer layer of the choroid and elsewhere It is supposed to be derived from the decomposition of hemoglobin'),
(59221, 'Melanism', 'The character of having a high degree of pigmentation as shown in dark skin eyes and hair'),
(59222, 'Melanistic', 'Affected with melanism of the nature of melanism'),
(59223, 'Melanite', 'A black variety of garnet'),
(59224, 'Melanochroi', 'A group of the human race including the dark whites'),
