(59226, 'Melanochroite', 'A mineral of a red or brownish or yellowish red color  It is a chromate of lead    called also phoenicocroite'),
(59227, 'Melanocomous', 'Having very dark or black hair black haired'),
(59228, 'Melanoma', 'A tumor containing dark pigment  Such tumors are usually malignant and often fatal'),
(59229, 'Melanorrhoea', 'An East Indian genus of large trees Melanorrh'),
(59230, 'Melanoscope', 'An instrument containing a combination of colored glasses such that they transmit only red light so that objects of other colors as green leaves appear black when seen through it  It is used for viewing colored flames to detect the presence of potassium lithium etc by the red light which they emit'),
(59231, 'Melanosis', 'The morbid deposition of black matter often of a malignant character causing pigmented tumors'),
(59232, 'Melanosperm', 'An alga of any kind that produces blackish spores or seed dust  The melanosperms include the rockweeds and all kinds of kelp'),
(59233, 'Melanotic', 'Melanistic'),
(59234, 'Melanotype', 'A positive picture produced with sensitized collodion on a smooth surface of black varnish coating a thin plate of iron also the process of making such a picture'),
(59235, 'Melanterite', 'A hydrous sulphate of iron of a green color and vitreous luster iron vitriol'),
(59236, 'Melanure', 'A small fish of the Mediterranean a gilthead See Gilthead a'),
(59237, 'Melanuric', 'Pertaining to or designating a complex nitrogenous acid obtained by decomposition of melam or of urea as a white crystalline powder    called also melanurenic acid'),
(59238, 'Melaphyre', 'Any one of several dark colored augitic eruptive rocks allied to basalt'),
(59239, 'Melasma', 'A dark discoloration of the skin usually local as Addisons melasma or Addisons disease'),
(59240, 'Melasses', 'See Molasses'),
(59241, 'Melassic', 'Pertaining to or designating an acid obtained from molasses or glucose and probably identical with saccharic acid also called D glucaric acid or tetrahydroxyadipic acid See Saccharic'),
(59242, 'Melastoma', 'A genus of evergreen tropical shrubs    so called from the black berries of some species which stain the mouth'),
(59243, 'Melastomaceous', 'Belonging to the order of which Melastoma is the type'),
(59244, 'melatonin', 'A hormone secreted by the pineal gland  Chemically it is N acety 5 methoxytryptamine  Research has indicated that there are daily rhythms in secretion of melatonin in particular due to the depressing effect on melatonin production by light received by the retina  Conversely it appears that melatonin may influence the circadian rhythms of animals  There is some experimental evidence that administration of melatonin may increase the amount of sleep in people with sleep disorders  However the evidence is not convincing and the effect is not profound  Nevertheless the deregulation of melatonin and its availability over the counter has led to many people taking melatonin to help sleep without consulting a physician'),
(59245, 'Melchite', 'One of a sect chiefly in Syria and Egypt which acknowledges the authority of the pope but adheres to the liturgy and ceremonies of the Eastern Church'),
(59246, 'Meld', 'In the game of pinochle to declare or announce for a score as to meld a sequence'),
(59247, 'Meleagrididae', 'A natural family of fowls including the turkeys and some extinct forms'),
(59248, 'Meleagrine', 'Of or pertaining to the genus Meleagris'),
(59249, 'Meleagris', 'A genus of American gallinaceous birds including the common turkey and the wild turkeys'),
(59250, 'Melena', 'See Melaena'),
(59251, 'Melene', 'An unsaturated hydrocarbon C30H60 of the ethylene series obtained from beeswax as a white scaly crystalline wax    called also melissene and melissylene'),
(59252, 'Melenite', 'An explosive of great destructive power    so called from its color which resembles honey'),
(59253, 'Meletin', 'See Quercitin'),
(59254, 'Melezitose', 'A variety of sugar isomeric with sucrose extracted from the manna of the larch Larix'),
(59255, 'Meliaceous', 'Pertaining to a natural order Meliacae of plants of which the genus Melia is the type It includes the mahogany and the Spanish cedar'),
(59256, 'Melibean', 'Alternately responsive as verses'),
(59257, 'Melic', 'Of or pertaining to song lyric tuneful'),
(59258, 'Melicerous', 'Consisting of or containing matter like honey    said of certain encysted tumors'),
(59259, 'Melic grass', 'A genus of grasses Melica of little agricultural importance'),
(59260, 'Melicotoon', 'See Melocoton'),
(59261, 'Melicratory', 'A meadlike drink'),
(59262, 'Melilite', 'A mineral occurring in small yellow crystals found in the lavas melilite basalt of Vesuvius and elsewhere'),
(59263, 'Melilot', 'Any species of Melilotus a genus of leguminous herbs having a vanillalike odor sweet clover harts clover The blue melilot Melilotus caerulea is used in Switzerland to give color and flavor to sapsago cheese'),
(59264, 'Melilotic', 'Of pertaining to or obtained from sweet clover or melilot specifically designating an acid of the aromatic series obtained from melilot as a white crystalline substance'),
(59265, 'Melinae', 'A subdivision of mammals not used in some classifications it includes the badgers'),
(59266, 'Meliorate', 'To make better to improve to ameliorate to soften to make more tolerable'),
