(59410, 'menhaden', 'An American marine fish Brevoortia tyrannus of the Herring family Clupeidae chiefly valuable for its oil and as a component of fertilizers    called also mossbunker bony fish chebog pogy hardhead whitefish etc'),
(59411, 'Menhir', 'A large stone set upright in olden times as a memorial or monument  Many of unknown date are found in Brittany and throughout Northern Europe'),
