(60070, 'Mica', 'The name of a group of minerals characterized by highly perfect cleavage so that they readily separate into very thin leaves more or less elastic  They differ widely in composition and vary in color from pale brown or yellow to green or black  The transparent forms are used in lanterns the doors of stoves etc being popularly called isinglass  Formerly called also cat silver and glimmer'),
