(60132, 'micromercurialism', 'A form of mercury poisoning resulting from long term exposure to low doses of mercury  The syndrome of micromercurialism involves complex symptoms of stress fatigue memory loss fine tremors muscular and reflex insufficiency and low blood pressure caused by accumulation of mercury in the system  A condition of hyperthermia is accompanied by a series of functional changes under the effects of mercury  The combined simultaneous effect of toxic action temperature and galvanic response infers a cycle of disintegration and change'),
(60133, 'Micromere', 'One of the smaller cells or blastomeres resulting from the complete segmentation of a telolecithal ovum'),
