(62138, 'Mosasaur', 'One of an extinct order of reptiles including Mosasaurus and allied genera See Mosasauria'),
(62139, 'Mosasauria', 'An order of large extinct marine reptiles found in the Cretaceous rocks especially in America  They were serpentlike in form and in having loosely articulated and dilatable jaws with large recurved teeth but they had paddlelike feet Some of them were over fifty feet long They are essentially fossil sea serpents with paddles Called also Pythonomarpha and Mosasauria'),
(62140, 'Mosasaurus', 'A genus of extinct marine reptiles allied to the lizards but having the body much elongated and the limbs in the form of paddles  The first known species nearly fifty feet in length was discovered in Cretaceous beds near Maestricht in the Netherlands'),
(62141, 'Moschatel', 'A plant of the genus Adoxa Adoxa moschatellina the flowers of which are pale green and have a faint musky smell  It is found in woods in all parts of Europe and is called also hollow root and musk crowfoot'),
