(62151, 'Mosque', 'A Muslim church or place of religious worship'),
(62152, 'Mosquito', 'Any one of various species of gnats of the genus Culex and allied genera  The females have a proboscis containing within the sheathlike labium six fine sharp needlelike organs with which they puncture the skin of man and animals to suck the blood  These bites when numerous cause in many persons considerable irritation and swelling with some pain  The larvae and pupae called wigglers are aquatic'),
(62153, 'mosquitofish', 'A silvery topminnow Gambusia affinis with rows of black spots of tropical North America and West Indies important in mosquito control'),
(62154, 'Moss', 'A cryptogamous plant of a cellular structure with distinct stem and simple leaves  The fruit is a small capsule usually opening by an apical lid and so discharging the spores  There are many species collectively termed Musci growing on the earth on rocks and trunks of trees etc and a few in running water'),
(62155, 'Mossback', 'A veteran partisan one who is so conservative in opinion that he may be likened to a stone or old tree covered with moss'),
