(63848, 'Neoplatonism', 'A pantheistic eclectic school of philosophy of which Plotinus was the chief a d 205 270 and which sought to reconcile the Platonic and Aristotelian systems with Oriental theosophy  It tended to mysticism and theurgy and was the last product of Greek philosophy'),
