(63882, 'nephrite', 'A hard compact mineral of a dark green color formerly worn as a remedy for diseases of the kidneys whence its name kidney stone a kind of jade  It varies in color from white to dark green  It is the more common and less valuable variety of jade the other being jadeite  Large deposits are found in Australia  Called also nephritic stone  See also Jade'),
