(67071, 'Oriolus', 'The type genus of the Oriolidae'),
(67072, 'Orion', 'A large and bright constellation on the equator between the stars Aldebaran and Sirius  It contains a remarkable nebula visible to the naked eye'),
(67073, 'Oriskany', 'Designating or pertaining to certain beds chiefly limestone characteristic of the latest period of the Silurian age'),
(67074, 'Orismological', 'Of or pertaining to orismology'),
(67075, 'Orismology', 'That department of natural history which treats of technical terms the science of defining technical terms'),
(67076, 'Orison', 'A prayer a supplication'),
(67077, 'Orisont', 'Horizon'),
(67078, 'Ork', 'See Orc'),
(67079, 'Orkneyan', 'Of or pertaining to the Orkney islands'),
(67080, 'Orleans', 'A cloth made of worsted and cotton    used for wearing apparel'),
(67081, 'Orlo', 'A wind instrument of music in use among the Spaniards'),
(67082, 'Orlop', 'The lowest deck of a vessel esp of a ship of war consisting of a platform laid over the beams in the hold on which the cables are coiled'),
(67083, 'Ormazd', 'The supreme deity the embodiment of the principle of good creator of the world source of light and guardian of mankind  He is the opponent of Ahriman the spirit of evil both being sprung from Eternity or according to another version Ahriman being the offspring of a moment of doubt on the part of Ormazd  Ormazd is attended by angels and archangels  He is represented as a bearded man inclosed in a winged circle a conception probably derived from the Assyrian representations of Ashur'),
(67084, 'Ormer', 'An abalone'),
(67085, 'ormolu', 'A variety of brass made to resemble gold by the use of less zinc and more copper in its composition than ordinary brass contains  Its golden color is often heightened by means of lacquer of some sort or by use of acids Called also mosaic gold'),
(67086, 'Ormosia', 'A genus of tropical shrubs and trees having usually odd pinnate leaves with large leaflets and pink to reddish wood'),
(67087, 'Ormuzd', 'The good principle or being of the ancient Persian religion same as Ormazd See also Ahriman'),
(67088, 'orn', 'To ornament to adorn'),
