(67221, 'Orthoscopic', 'Giving an image in correct or normal proportions giving a flat field of view as an orthoscopic eyepiece'),
(67222, 'Orthosilicic', 'Designating the form of silicic acid having the normal or highest number of hydroxyl groups'),
(67223, 'Orthospermous', 'Having the seeds straight as in the fruits of some umbelliferous plants    opposed to coelospermous'),
(67224, 'Orthostade', 'A chiton or loose ungirded tunic falling in straight folds'),
(67225, 'Orthostichy', 'A longitudinal rank or row of leaves along a stem'),
(67226, 'Orthotomic', 'Cutting at right angles'),
(67227, 'Orthotomous', 'Having two cleavages at right angles with one another'),
(67228, 'Orthotomy', 'The property of cutting at right angles'),
(67229, 'Orthotone', 'Retaining the accent not enclitic    said of certain indefinite pronouns and adverbs when used interrogatively which when not so used are ordinarilly enclitic'),
(67230, 'Orthotropal', 'Having the axis of an ovule or seed straight from the hilum and chalaza to the orifice or the micropyle atropous'),
(67231, 'Orthotropic', 'Having the longer axis vertical    said of erect stems'),
(67232, 'Orthoxylene', 'That variety of xylene C6H4CH32 in which the two methyl groups are in the ortho position a colorless liquid combustible hydrocarbon resembling benzene'),
(67233, 'Ortive', 'Of or relating to the time or act of rising eastern as the ortive amplitude of a planet'),
(67234, 'Ortolan', 'A European singing bird Emberiza hortulana about the size of the lark with black wings  It is esteemed delicious food when fattened  Called also bunting'),
(67235, 'Ortygan', 'One of several species of East Indian birds of the genera Ortygis and Hemipodius  They resemble quails but lack the hind toe See Turnix'),
(67236, 'Orval', 'A kind of sage Salvia Horminum'),
(67237, 'Orvet', 'The blindworm'),
(67238, 'Orvietan', 'A kind of antidote for poisons a counter poison formerly in vogue'),
(67239, ' ory', 'An adjective suffix meaning of or pertaining to serving for as in auditory pertaining to or serving for hearing prohibitory amendatory etc'),
(67240, 'Oryal', 'See Oriel'),
(67241, 'Oryctere', 'The aard vark Orycteropus afer'),
(67242, 'Orycterope', 'Same as Oryctere the aardvark Orycteropus afer'),
(67243, 'Oryctognosy', 'Mineralogy'),
(67244, 'Oryctography', 'Description of fossils'),
(67245, 'Oryctological', 'Of or pertaining to oryctology'),
(67246, 'Oryctologist', 'One versed in oryctology'),
(67247, 'Oryctology', 'An old name for paleontology'),
(67248, 'Oryx', 'A genus of African antelopes which includes the gemsbok the leucoryx the bisa antelope Oryx beisa and the beatrix antelope Oryx beatrix of Arabia'),
(67249, 'Oryza', 'A genus of grasses including the rice plant rice'),
(67250, 'Oryzomys', 'A genus of rodents including the rice rats'),
(67251, 'Oryzopsis', 'A genus of grasses incluiding rice grass'),
(67252, 'orzo', 'Pasta shaped like pearls of barley frequently prepared with lamb in Greek cuisine'),
(67253, 'Os', 'A bone'),
(67254, 'Osage', 'A tributary of the Missouri River'),
(67255, 'Osage orange', 'An ornamental tree of the genus Maclura Maclura aurantiaca closely allied to the mulberry Morus also its fruit  The tree was first found in the country of the Osage Indians and bears a hard and inedible fruit of an orangelike appearance See Bois darc'),
(67256, 'Osages', 'A tribe of southern Sioux Indians now living in the Indian Territory'),
(67257, 'Osanne', 'Hosanna'),
(67258, 'Osar', 'See 3d Os'),
(67259, 'Oscan', 'Of or pertaining to the Osci a primitive people of Campania a province of ancient Italy'),
(67260, 'Oscillancy', 'The state of oscillating a seesaw kind of motion'),
(67261, 'Oscillaria', 'A genus of dark green or purplish black filamentous fresh water algae the threads of which have an automatic swaying or crawling motion Called also Oscillatoria'),
(67262, 'Oscillating', 'That oscillates vibrating swinging'),
(67263, 'Oscillating current', 'A current alternating in direction'),
(67264, 'Oscillative', 'Tending to oscillate vibratory'),
(67265, 'oscillator', 'One that oscillates'),
(67266, 'Oscillatoria', 'Same as Oscillaria'),
(67267, 'Oscillatory', 'Moving or characterized by motion backward and forward like a pendulum swinging oscillating vibratory as oscillatory motion'),
(67268, 'Oscillogram', 'An autographic record made by an oscillograph'),
(67269, 'oscillograph', 'a device for making a record of the wave forms of fluctuating '),
(67270, 'Oscillometer', 'An instrument for measuring the angle through which a ship rolls or pitches at sea'),
(67271, 'oscilloscope', 'An electronic measuring instrument which provides a visual representation of the time variation of electrical quantities such as voltage or current  It may be used to measure the shape of a voltage pulse or the frequency of an oscillating voltage  It can also be used to measure properties of other physical variables such as sound or light intensity if they can be translated into electrical voltage or current'),
(67272, 'Oscine', 'Relating to the Oscines'),
(67273, 'Oscines', 'Singing birds a group of the Passeres having numerous syringeal muscles conferring musical ability'),
(67274, 'Oscinian', 'One of the Oscines or singing birds'),
(67275, 'Oscinine', 'Of or pertaining to the Oscines'),
(67276, 'Oscitant', 'Yawning gaping'),
(67277, 'Oscitantly', 'In an oscitant manner'),
(67278, 'Oscitate', 'To gape to yawn'),
(67279, 'Oscitation', 'The act of yawning or gaping'),
(67280, 'Osculate', 'To kiss one another to kiss'),
(67281, 'Osculation', 'The act of kissing a kiss'),
(67282, 'Osculatory', 'Of or pertaining to kissing kissing'),
(67283, 'Osculatrix', 'A curve whose contact with a given curve at a given point is of a higher order or involves the equality of a greater number of successive differential coefficients of the ordinates of the curves taken at that point than that of any other curve of the same kind'),
(67284, 'Oscule', 'One of the excurrent apertures of sponges'),
(67285, 'Osculum', 'Same as Oscule'),
(67286, 'Osier', 'A kind of willow Salix viminalis growing in wet places in Europe and Asia and introduced into North America  It is considered the best of the willows for basket work  The name is sometimes given to any kind of willow'),
(67287, 'Osiered', 'Covered or adorned with osiers as osiered banks'),
(67288, 'Osiery', 'An osier bed'),
(67289, 'Osiris', 'One of the principal divinities of Egypt the brother and husband of Isis  He was figured as a mummy wearing the royal cap of Upper Egypt and was symbolized by the sacred bull called Apis  Cf Serapis'),
(67290, 'Osmanli', 'A Turkish official one of the dominant tribe of Turks loosely any Turk'),
(67291, 'Osmate', 'A salt of osmic acid'),
(67292, 'Osmaterium', 'One of a pair of scent organs which the larvae of certain butterflies emit from the first body segment either above or below'),
(67293, 'Osmazome', 'A substance formerly supposed to give to soup and broth their characteristic odor and probably consisting of one or several of the class of nitrogenous substances which are called extractives'),
(67294, 'Osmiamate', 'A salt of osmiamic acid'),
(67295, 'Osmiamic', 'Of pertaining to or designating a nitrogenous acid of osmium H2N2Os2O5 forming a well known series of yellow salts'),
(67296, 'Osmic', 'Pertaining to derived from or containing osmium specifically designating those compounds in which it has a valence higher than in other lower compounds as osmic oxide'),
(67297, 'Osmidrosis', 'The secretion of fetid sweat'),
(67298, 'Osmious', 'Denoting those compounds of osmium in which the element has a valence relatively lower than in the osmic compounds as osmious chloride'),
(67299, 'osmite', 'A salt of osmious acid'),
(67300, 'osmium', 'A rare metallic element of the platinum group with atomic number 76  It is found native as an alloy in platinum ore and in iridosmine  It is a hard infusible bluish or grayish white metal and the heaviest substance known  Its tetroxide is used in histological experiments to stain tissues Symbol Os  Atomic weight 1902  Specific gravity 22477'),
(67301, 'osmogene', 'An apparatus consisting of a number of cells whose sides are of parchment paper for conducting the process of osmosis  It is used especially in sugar refining to remove potassium salts from the molasses'),
(67302, 'osmograph', 'An instrument for recording the height of the liquid in an endosmometer or for registering osmotic pressures'),
(67303, 'osmometer', 'An instrument for measuring the amount of osmotic action in different liquids'),
(67304, 'Osmometry', 'The study of osmosis by means of the osmometer'),
(67305, 'Osmose', 'The tendency in fluids to mix or become equably diffused when in contact  Same as osmosis which see'),
