(68931, 'Pallium', 'A large square woolen cloak which enveloped the whole person worn by the Greeks and by certain Romans  It is the Roman name of a Greek garment'),
(68932, 'Pall mall', 'A game formerly common in England in which a wooden ball was driven with a mallet through an elevated hoop or ring of iron  The name was also given to the mallet used to the place where the game was played and to the street in London still called Pall Mall'),
