(69914, 'Pass', 'To go to move to proceed to be moved or transferred from one point to another to make a transit    usually with a following adverb or adverbal phrase defining the kind or manner of motion as to pass on by out in etc to pass swiftly directly smoothly etc to pass to the rear under the yoke over the bridge across the field beyond the border etc'),
