(69954, 'Passionist', 'A member of a religious order founded in Italy in 1737 and introduced into the United States in 1852  The members of the order unite the austerities of the Trappists with the activity and zeal of the Jesuits and Lazarists  Called also Barefooted Clerks of the Most Holy Cross'),
