(72327, 'Phthalate', 'A salt of phthalic acid'),
(72328, 'Phthalein', 'One of a series of artificial organic dyes made as condensation products of the phenols with phthalic acid and well represented by phenolphthalein  Their alkaline solutions are fluorescent'),
(72329, 'Phthalic', 'Pertaining to or designating a dibasic acid obtained by the oxidation of naphthalene and allied substances'),
(72330, 'Phthalide', 'A lactone C8H6O2 obtained as a white crystalline substance by reduction of phthalyl chloride and other processes hence by extension any one of the series of which phthalide proper is the type'),
(72331, 'Phthalimide', 'An imido derivative of phthalic acid obtained as a white crystalline substance C6H4CO2NH which has itself like succinimide acid properties and forms a series of salts  Cf Imido acid under Imido'),
(72332, 'Phthalin', 'A colorless crystalline substance obtained by reduction from phthalein into which it is easily converted by oxidation hence any one of the series of which phthalin proper is the type'),
(72333, 'Phthalyl', 'The hypothetical radical of phthalic acid'),
(72334, 'Phthiriasis', 'A disease morbus pediculous consisting in the excessive multiplication of lice on the human body'),
(72335, 'Phthisic', 'Same as Phthisis'),
(72336, 'Phthisical', 'Of or pertaining to phthisis affected with phthisis wasting consumptive'),
(72337, 'Phthisicky', 'Having phthisis or some symptom of it as difficulty in breathing'),
(72338, 'Phthisiology', 'A treatise on phthisis'),
(72339, 'Phthisipneumonia', 'Pulmonary consumption tuberculosis of the lungs'),
(72340, 'phthisis', 'A wasting or consumption of the tissues  The term is now obsolete it was once applied to many wasting diseases but in the early 1900s became restricted to tuberculosis of the lungs pulmonary phthisis or consumption See Consumption'),
(72341, 'Phthongal', 'Formed into or characterized by voice vocalized    said of all the vowels and the semivowels also of the vocal or sonant consonants g d b l r v z etc'),
(72342, 'Phthongometer', 'An instrument for measuring vocal sounds'),
(72343, 'phtor', 'Fluorine'),
(72344, 'Phycite', 'See Erythrite 1'),
(72345, 'Phycochrome', 'A bluish green coloring matter of certain alg'),
(72346, 'Phycocyanin', 'A blue coloring matter found in certain algae'),
(72347, 'Phycoerythrin', 'A red coloring matter found in algae of the subclass Florideae'),
(72348, 'Phycography', 'A description of seaweeds'),
(72349, 'Phycology', 'The science of algae or seaweeds algology'),
(72350, 'Phycomater', 'A gelatin in which the algae spores have been supposed to vegetate'),
(72351, 'Phycomycetes', 'A large important class of parasitic or saprophytic fungi the algal or algalike fungi  The plant body ranges from an undifferentiated mass of protoplasm to a well developed and much branched mycelium  Reproduction is mainly sexual by the formation of conidia or sporangia but the group shows every form of transition from this method through simple conjugation to perfect sexual reproduction by egg and sperm in the higher forms'),
(72352, 'Phycoph', 'A brown coloring matter found in certain alg'),
(72353, 'Phycoxanthin', 'A yellowish coloring matter found in certain algae'),
(72354, 'Phylacter', 'A phylactery'),
(72355, 'Phylactered', 'Wearing a phylactery'),
(72356, 'Phylacteric', 'Of or pertaining to phylacteries'),
(72357, 'Phylactery', 'Any charm or amulet worn as a preservative from danger or disease'),
(72358, 'Phylactocarp', 'A branch of a plumularian hydroid specially modified in structure for the protection of the gonothec'),
(72359, 'Phylactol', 'An order of fresh water Bryozoa in which the tentacles are arranged on a horseshoe shaped lophophore and the mouth is covered by an epistome  Called also Lophopoda and hippocrepians'),
(72360, 'Phylactolema', 'Same as Phylactol'),
(72361, 'Phylarch', 'The chief of a phyle or tribe'),
(72362, 'Phylarchy', 'The office of a phylarch government of a class or tribe'),
(72363, 'Phyle', 'A local division of the people in ancient Athens a clan a tribe'),
(72364, 'Phyllite', 'A mineral related to ottrelite'),
(72365, 'Phyllo ', 'A combining form from Gr fyllon a leaf as phyllopod phyllotaxy'),
(72366, 'Phyllobranchia', 'A crustacean gill composed of lamellae'),
(72367, 'phylloclade', 'A flattened stem or branch which more or less resembles a leaf and performs the function of a leaf as regards respiration and assimilation'),
(72368, 'Phyllocladus', 'A genus consisting of celery pine'),
(72369, 'Phyllocyanin', 'A blue coloring matter extracted from chlorophyll'),
(72370, 'Phyllocyst', 'The cavity of a hydrophyllium'),
(72371, 'Phyllode', 'Same as Phyllodium'),
(72372, 'Phyllodineous', 'Having phyllodia relating to phyllodia'),
(72373, 'Phyllodium', 'A petiole dilated into the form of a blade and usually with vertical edges as in the Australian acacias'),
(72374, 'Phyllody', 'A retrograde metamorphosis of the floral organs to the condition of leaves'),
(72375, 'Phylloid', 'Resembling a leaf'),
(72376, 'Phyllomania', 'An abnormal or excessive production of leaves'),
(72377, 'phyllome', 'A foliar part of a plant any organ homologous with a leaf or produced by metamorphosis of a leaf'),
(72378, 'Phyllomorphosis', 'The succession and variation of leaves during different seasons'),
(72379, 'Phyllophagan', 'One of a group of marsupials including the phalangists'),
(72380, 'Phyllophagous', 'Substituting on leaves leaf eating'),
(72381, 'Phyllophorous', 'Leaf bearing producing leaves'),
(72382, 'phyllopod', 'One of the Phyllopoda Also used adjectively'),
(72383, 'Phyllopoda', 'An order of Entomostraca including a large number of species most of which live in fresh water  They have flattened or leaflike legs often very numerous which they use in swimming Called also Branchiopoda'),
(72384, 'Phyllopodous', 'Of or pertaining to the Phyllopoda'),
(72385, 'Phyllorhine', 'Of or pertaining to Phyllorhina and other related genera of bats that have a leaflike membrane around the nostrils'),
(72386, 'Phyllosoma', 'The larva of the spiny lobsters Palinurus and allied genera  Its body is remarkably thin flat and transparent the legs are very long  Called also glass crab and glass shrimp'),
(72387, 'Phyllostome', 'Any bat of the genus Phyllostoma or allied genera having large membranes around the mouth and nose a nose leaf bat'),
(72388, 'Phyllostomid', 'A phyllostome'),
(72389, 'Phyllotactic', 'Of or pertaining to phyllotaxy'),
(72390, 'Phyllotaxy', 'The order or arrangement of leaves on the stem the science of the relative position of leaves'),
(72391, 'Phyllous', 'Homologous with a leaf as the sepals petals stamens and pistils are phyllous organs'),
(72392, 'Phylloxanthin', 'A yellow coloring matter extracted from chlorophyll'),
(72393, 'Phylloxera', 'A small hemipterous insect Phylloxera vastatrix allied to the aphids  It attacks the roots and leaves of the grapevine doing great damage especially in Europe'),
(72394, 'Phylloxeridae', 'A natural family consisting of the plant lice'),
(72395, 'phylogenesis', 'The history of genealogical development the sequence of events involved in the evolutionary development of a species or taxonomic group of organisms the historic exolution of the phylon or tribe in distinction from ontogeny or the development of the individual organism and from biogenesis or life development generally'),
(72396, 'Phylogenetic', 'Relating to phylogenesis or the evolutionary history of a type of organism'),
(72397, 'Phylon', 'A tribe'),
(72398, 'Phylum', 'One of the larger divisions of the animal kingdom a branch a grand division'),
(72399, 'Phyma', 'A tubercle on any external part of the body'),
(72400, 'Physa', 'A genus of fresh water Pulmonifera having reversed spiral shells See Pond snail under Pond'),
(72401, 'Physalia', 'A genus of large oceanic Siphonophora which includes the Portuguese man of war'),
(72402, 'Physali', 'An order of Siphonophora which includes Physalia'),
(72403, 'Physaria', 'A small genus of Western North American herbs similar to Lesquerella the bladderpods'),
(72404, 'Physemaria', 'A group of simple marine organisms usually classed as the lowest of the sponges They have inflated hollow bodies'),
(72405, 'Physeter', 'The genus that includes the sperm whale Physeter macrocephalus'),
(72406, 'Physeteridae', 'A natural family of marine mammals that includes the sperm whales'),
(72407, 'Physianthropy', 'The philosophy of human life or the doctrine of the constitution and diseases of man and their remedies'),
(72408, 'physiatrics', 'Therapy that use physical agents exercise and massage and so on'),
(72409, 'Physic', 'The art of healing diseases the science of medicine the theory or practice of medicine    an archaic term superseded by medicine'),
(72410, 'Physical', 'Of or pertaining to nature as including all created existences in accordance with the laws of nature also of or relating to natural or material things or to the bodily structure as opposed to things mental moral spiritual or imaginary material natural as armies and navies are the physical force of a nation the body is the physical part of man'),
(72411, 'physicalism', 'The doctrine that matter is the only reality'),
(72412, 'physicality', 'A preoccupation with satisfaction of physical drives and appetites    of people'),
(72413, 'Physically', 'In a physical manner according to the laws of nature or physics by physical force not morally'),
(72414, 'physicalness', 'The quality of being physical consisting of matter materiality'),
(72415, 'Physician', 'A person skilled in medicine or the art of healing especially one trained and licensed to treat illness and prescribe medicines a doctor of medicine'),
(72416, 'Physicianed', 'Licensed as a physician'),
(72417, 'Physicism', 'The tendency of the mind toward or its preoccupation with physical phenomena materialism in philosophy and religion'),
(72418, 'Physicist', 'One versed in physics'),
(72419, 'Physicking', 'p pr  vb n fr Physic v t'),
(72420, 'Physico ', 'A combining form denoting relation to or dependence upon natural causes or the science of physics'),
(72421, 'Physicochemical', 'Involving the principles of both physics and chemistry dependent on or produced by the joint action of physical and chemical agencies'),
(72422, 'Physicologic', 'Logic illustrated by physics'),
(72423, 'Physicological', 'Of or pertaining to physicologic'),
(72424, 'Physicology', 'Physics'),
(72425, 'Physico mathematics', 'Mixed mathematics'),
(72426, 'Physico philosophy', 'The philosophy of nature'),
(72427, 'Physico theology', 'Theology or divinity illustrated or enforced by physics or natural philosophy'),
(72428, 'Physics', 'The science of nature or of natural objects that branch of science which treats of the laws and properties of matter and the forces acting upon it especially that department of natural science which treats of the causes as gravitation heat light magnetism electricity etc that modify the general properties of bodies natural philosophy'),
(72429, 'Physiocrat', 'One of the followers of Quesnay of France who in the 18th century founded a system of political economy based upon the supremacy of natural order'),
(72430, 'Physiogeny', 'The germ history of the functions or the history of the development of vital activities in the individual being one of the branches of ontogeny See Morphogeny'),
(72431, 'Physiognomer', 'Physiognomist'),
(72432, 'Physiognomic', 'Of or pertaining to physiognomy according with the principles of physiognomy'),
(72433, 'Physiognomist', 'Same as Physiognomy 1'),
(72434, 'Physiognomize', 'To observe and study the physiognomy of'),
