(72935, 'Pintsch gas', 'A kind of oil gas extensively used for lighting railroad cars which carry it in compressed form'),
(72936, 'Pinule', 'One of the sights of an astrolabe'),
(72937, 'Pinus', 'A large genus of evergreen coniferous trees mostly found in the northern hemisphere The genus formerly included the firs spruces larches and hemlocks but is now limited to those trees which have the primary leaves of the branchlets reduced to mere scales and the secondary ones pine needles acicular and usually in fascicles of two to seven See Pine'),
(72938, 'Pinweed', 'Any plant of the genus Lechea low North American herbs with branching stems and very small and abundant leaves and flowers'),
(72939, 'Pinworm', 'A small nematoid worm Oxyurus vermicularis which is parasitic chiefly in the rectum of man It is most common in children and aged persons'),
(72940, 'Pinxit', 'A word appended to the artists name or initials on a painting or engraved copy of a painting as Rubens pinxit Rubens painted this'),
