(76964, 'Pteroceras', 'A genus of large marine gastropods having the outer border of the lip divided into lobes    called also scorpion shell'),
(76965, 'Pterocletes', 'A division of birds including the sand grouse  They are in some respects intermediate between the pigeons and true grouse  Called also Pteroclomorph'),
(76966, 'Pterodactyl', 'An extinct flying reptile one of the Pterosauria See Illustration in Appendix'),
(76967, 'Pterodactyli', 'Same as Pterosauria'),
(76968, 'Pteroglossal', 'Having the tongue finely notched along the sides so as to have a featherlike appearance as the toucans'),
