(78364, 'radar', 'An electronic device designed to detect objects at a distance and determine their distance from the device by transmitting a pulse of radio waves and measuring the time required for the echo of the pulse to return to the emitting device as the radar showed a plane approaching rapidly  For more information of radar see the article What is Radar'),
