(79531, 'Redthroat', 'A small Australian singing bird Phyrrholaemus brunneus The upper parts are brown the center of the throat red'),
(79532, 'Redtop', 'A kind of grass Agrostis vulgaris highly valued in the United States for pasturage and hay for cattle    called also English grass and in some localities herds grass See Illustration in Appendix The tall redtop is Triodia seslerioides'),
(79533, 'Redub', 'To refit to repair or make reparation for hence to repay or requite'),
