(81987, 'Romancist', 'A romancer'),
(81988, 'Romancy', 'Romantic'),
(81989, 'Romanesque', 'Somewhat resembling the Roman    applied sometimes to the debased style of the later Roman empire but esp to the more developed architecture prevailing from the 8th century to the 12th'),
