(82610, 'Rusk', 'A kind of light soft bread made with yeast and eggs often toasted or crisped in an oven or a kind of sweetened biscuit'),
(82611, 'Rusma', 'A depilatory made of orpiment and quicklime and used by the Turks See Rhusma'),
(82612, 'Russ', 'A Russian or the Russians'),
(82613, 'Russet', 'Of a reddish brown color or by some called a red gray of the color composed of blue red and yellow in equal strength but unequal proportions namely two parts of red to one each of blue and yellow also of a yellowish brown color'),
(82614, 'Russeting', 'See Russet n 2 and 4'),
(82615, 'Russety', 'Of a russet color russet'),
(82616, 'Russia', 'A country of Europe and Asia'),
(82617, 'Russian', 'Of or pertaining to Russia its inhabitants or language'),
(82618, 'Russian Church', 'The established church of the Russian empire up to the revolution of 1917 at which time the ruling Communist party tried to suppress all religious worship  The czar was the nominal head of the church but he never claimed the right of deciding questions of theology and dogma It still forms a portion by far the largest of the Orthodox Eastern Church and is governed by the Patriarch and the Holy Synod In 1988 the church with official approval celebrated the 1000 year anniversary of the baptism of Russia  After breakup of the Soviet Union in 1991 the Russian Church began to regain some its old influence in Russian life and the government turned over some of the confiscated churches back to church control  The Russian Church was recognized anew as the official church of Russia with special priveleges by an act of the Russian Duma in 1997  The Metropolitan of Moscow as Patriarch of the church is regarded as the first among equals in order of deference among bishops of the church'),
(82619, 'Russianize', 'To make Russian or more or less like the Russians as to Russianize the Poles'),
(82620, 'Russian roulette', 'An act of bravado played by loading one bullet into one chamber of a revolver in which the cylinder has five or six positions spinning the cylinder thus moving the bullet randomly to one of the six positions of the cylinder pointing the gun to ones head and pulling the trigger  If the bullet is in firing position the player is usually killed Such a game may be played on a dare or in some places as part of a gamble'),
(82621, 'Russification', 'The act or process of Russifying or the state of being Russified'),
(82622, 'Russify', 'To Russianize as to Russify conquered tribes'),
(82623, 'Russophile', 'One who not being a Russian favors Russian policy and aggrandizement'),
(82624, 'Russophobe', 'One who dreads Russia or Russian influence'),
(82625, 'Russophobia', 'Morbid dread of Russia or of Russian influence'),
(82626, 'Rust', 'The reddish yellow coating formed on iron when exposed to moist air consisting of ferric oxide or hydroxide hence by extension any metallic film of corrosion'),
(82627, 'Rustful', 'Full of rust resembling rust causing rust rusty'),
(82628, 'Rustic', 'Of or pertaining to the country rural as the rustic gods of antiquity'),
(82629, 'Rustical', 'Rustic'),
(82630, 'Rusticate', 'To go into or reside in the country to ruralize'),
(82631, 'Rusticated', 'Resembling rustic work See Rustic work a under Rustic'),
(82632, 'Rustication', 'The act of rusticating or the state of being rusticated specifically the punishment of a student for some offense by compelling him to leave the institution for a time'),
(82633, 'Rusticity', 'The quality or state of being rustic rustic manners rudeness simplicity artlessness'),
(82634, 'Rusticly', 'In a rustic manner rustically'),
(82635, 'Rustily', 'In a rusty state'),
(82636, 'Rustiness', 'The quality or state of being rusty');
