(83095, 'Saltmouth', 'A wide mouthed bottle with glass stopper for holding chemicals especially crystallized salts'),
(83096, 'Saltness', 'The quality or state of being salt or impregnated with salt salt taste as the saltness of sea water  In the sense of having salt content saltiness is more commonly used'),
(83097, 'Saltpeter', 'Potassium nitrate niter a white crystalline substance KNO3 having a cooling saline taste obtained by leaching from certain soils in which it is produced by the process of nitrification see Nitrification 2 It is a strong oxidizer is the chief constituent of gunpowder and is also used as an antiseptic in curing meat and in medicine as a diuretic diaphoretic and refrigerant'),
(83098, 'Saltpetrous', 'Pertaining to saltpeter or partaking of its qualities impregnated with saltpeter'),
(83099, 'Salt rheum', 'A popular name esp in the United States for various cutaneous eruptions particularly for those of eczema See Eczema'),
(83100, 'Saltwort', 'A name given to several plants which grow on the seashore as the Batis maritima and the glasswort See Glasswort'),
(83101, 'Salty', 'Containing salt tasting of salt saltish as the salty sea the potatoes are too salty'),
(83102, 'Salubrious', 'Favorable to health healthful promoting health as salubrious air water or climate'),
(83103, 'Salubrity', 'The quality of being salubrious favorableness to the preservation of health salubriousness wholesomeness healthfulness as the salubrity of the air of a country or a climate'),
(83104, 'Salue', 'To salute'),
(83105, 'Salutary', 'Wholesome healthful promoting health as salutary exercise'),
(83106, 'Salutation', 'The act of saluting or paying respect or reverence by the customary words or actions the act of greeting or expressing good will or courtesy also that which is uttered or done in saluting or greeting'),
(83107, 'Salutatorian', 'The student who pronounces the salutatory oration at the annual Commencement or like exercises of a college    an honor commonly assigned to that member of the graduating class who ranks second in scholarship'),
