(85760, 'Sequin', 'An old gold coin of Italy and Turkey It was first struck at Venice about the end of the 13th century and afterward in the other Italian cities and by the Levant trade was introduced into Turkey It is worth about 9s 3d sterling or about 225 The different kinds vary somewhat in value'),
