(88101, 'Snails', 'Gods nails or His nails that is the nails with which the Savior was fastened to the cross    an ancient form of oath corresponding to Ods bodikins dim of body ie Gods dear body'),
(88102, 'Snake', 'Any species of the order Ophidia an ophidian a serpent whether harmless or venomous See Ophidia and Serpent'),
(88103, 'Snakebird', 'Any one of four species of aquatic birds of the genus Anhinga or Plotus  They are allied to the gannets and cormorants but have very long slender flexible necks and sharp bills'),
(88104, 'Snakefish', 'The band fish'),
(88105, 'Snakehead', 'A loose bent up end of one of the strap rails or flat rails formerly used on American railroads It was sometimes so bent by the passage of a train as to slip over a wheel and pierce the bottom of a car'),
(88106, 'Snakeneck', 'The snakebird 1'),
(88107, 'Snakeroot', 'Any one of several plants of different genera and species most of which are or were formerly reputed to be efficacious as remedies for the bites of serpents also the roots of any of these');
