(89524, 'Spinous', 'Spinose thorny'),
(89525, 'Spinozism', 'The form of Pantheism taught by Benedict Spinoza that there is but one substance or infinite essence in the universe of which the so called material and spiritual beings and phenomena are only modes and that one this one substance is God'),
