(90780, 'Stibiconite', 'A native oxide of antimony occurring in masses of a yellow color'),
(90781, 'Stibine', 'Antimony hydride or hydrogen antimonide a colorless gas produced by the action of nascent hydrogen on antimony It has a characteristic odor and burns with a characteristic greenish flame Formerly called also antimoniureted hydrogen'),
