(92402, 'Sulkily', 'In a sulky manner'),
(92403, 'Sulkiness', 'The quality or state of being sulky sullenness moroseness as sulkiness of disposition'),
(92404, 'Sulks', 'The condition of being sulky a sulky mood or humor as to be in the sulks'),
(92405, 'Sulky', 'Moodly silent sullen sour obstinate morose splenetic'),
(92406, 'Sull', 'A plow'),
(92407, 'Sullage', 'Drainage of filth filth collected from the street or highway sewage'),
(92408, 'Sullen', 'Lonely solitary desolate'),
(92409, 'Sullevate', 'To rouse to excite'),
(92410, 'Sulliage', 'Foulness filth'),
(92411, 'Sully', 'To soil to dirty to spot to tarnish to stain to darken    used literally and figuratively as to sully a sword to sully a persons reputation'),
(92412, 'Sulphacid', 'An acid in which to a greater or less extent sulphur plays a part analogous to that of oxygen in an oxyacid thus thiosulphuric and sulpharsenic acids are sulphacids    called also sulphoacid See the Note under Acid n 2'),
(92413, 'Sulphamate', 'A salt of sulphamic acid'),
