(93510, 'Sym ', 'See Syn '),
(93511, 'Symar', 'See Simar'),
(93512, 'Symbal', 'See Cimbal'),
(93513, 'Symbiosis', 'The living together in more or less imitative association or even close union of two dissimilar organisms In a broad sense the term includes parasitism or antagonistic symbiosis or antipathetic symbiosis in which the association is disadvantageous or destructive to one of the organisms but ordinarily it is used of cases where the association is advantageous or often necessary to one or both and not harmful to either When there is bodily union in extreme cases so close that the two form practically a single body as in the union of algae and fungi to form lichens and in the inclusion of algae in radiolarians it is called conjunctive symbiosis if there is no actual union of the organisms as in the association of ants with myrmecophytes disjunctive symbiosis'),
(93514, 'Symbiotic', 'Pertaining to or characterized by or living in a state of symbiosis'),
(93515, 'Symbol', 'A visible sign or representation of an idea anything which suggests an idea or quality or another thing as by resemblance or by convention an emblem a representation a type a figure as the lion is the symbol of courage the lamb is the symbol of meekness or patience'),
(93516, 'Symbolic', 'See Symbolics'),
(93517, 'Symbolics', 'The study of ancient symbols'),
(93518, 'Symbolism', 'The act of symbolizing or the state of being symbolized as symbolism in Christian art is the representation of truth virtues vices etc by emblematic colors signs and forms'),
(93519, 'Symbolist', 'One who employs symbols'),
(93520, 'Symbolistic', 'Characterized by the use of symbols as symbolistic poetry'),
(93521, 'Symbolization', 'The act of symbolizing symbolical representation'),
(93522, 'Symbolize', 'To have a resemblance of qualities or properties to correspond to harmonize'),
(93523, 'Symbolizer', 'One who symbolizes'),
(93524, 'Symbological', 'Pertaining to a symbology versed in or characterized by symbology'),
(93525, 'Symbologist', 'One who practices or who is versed in symbology'),
(93526, 'Symbology', 'The art of expressing by symbols'),
(93527, 'Symbranchii', 'An order of slender eel like fishes having the gill openings confluent beneath the neck The pectoral arch is generally attached to the skull and the entire margin of the upper jaw is formed by the premaxillary Called also Symbranchia'),
(93528, 'Symmetral', 'Commensurable symmetrical'),
