(94526, 'Tectibranchiata', 'An order or suborder of gastropod Mollusca in which the gills are usually situated on one side of the back and protected by a fold of the mantle  When there is a shell it is usually thin and delicate and often rudimentary The aplysias and the bubble shells are examples'),
