(94528, 'Tectly', 'Covertly privately secretly'),
(94529, 'Tectology', 'A division of morphology created by Haeckel the science of organic individuality constituting the purely structural portion of morphology in which the organism is regarded as composed of organic individuals of different orders each organ being considered an individual See Promorphology and Morphon'),
(94530, 'Tectonic', 'Of or pertaining to building or construction architectural'),
(94531, 'Tectonics', 'The science or the art by which implements vessels dwellings or other edifices are constructed both agreeably to the end for which they are designed and in conformity with artistic sentiments and ideas'),
