(94583, 'Teguexin', 'A large South American lizard Tejus teguexin It becomes three or four feet long and is blackish above marked with yellowish spots of various sizes It feeds upon fruits insects reptiles young birds and birds eggs The closely allied species Tejus rufescens is called red teguexin'),
