(95570, 'Thermochemistry', 'That branch of chemical science which includes the investigation of the various relations existing between chemical action and that manifestation of force termed heat or the determination of the heat evolved by or employed in chemical actions'),
(95571, 'Thermochroic', 'Pertaining to or designating heat rays that have undergone selective absorption and are therefore analogous to colored light rays'),
