(95968, 'Throwing', 'a  n from Throw v'),
(95969, 'Throwing stick', 'An instrument  used by various savage races for throwing a spear    called also throw stick and spear thrower  One end of the stick receives the butt of the spear as upon a hook or thong and the other end is grasped with the hand which also holds the spear toward the middle above it with the finger and thumb the effect being to bring the place of support nearer the center of the spear and practically lengthen the arm in the act of throwing  In Mexico one such device is called the atlatl'),
(95970, 'Thrown', 'a  p p from Throw v'),
