(95991, 'Thuggery', 'Thuggee'),
(95992, 'Thuja', 'A genus of evergreen trees thickly branched remarkable for the distichous arrangement of their branches and having scalelike closely imbricated or compressed leaves'),
(95993, 'thujone', 'An oil C10H16O the chief constituent of cedar leaf oil thuja oil which is obtained from the northern white cedar arbor vitae Thuja occidentalis or the western Red Cedar Thuja plicatis  It is a stimulant similar to camphor  It is also called thujol thuyol absinthol thuyone tanacetol and tanacetone'),
(95994, 'Thule', 'The name given by ancient geographers to the northernmost part of the habitable world  According to some this land was Norway according to others Iceland or more probably Mainland the largest of the Shetland islands hence the Latin phrase ultima Thule farthest Thule'),
(95995, 'Thulia', 'Oxide of thulium'),
(95996, 'Thulium', 'A rare metallic element of the lanthanide group having atomic number 69 and atomic weight 16893  It is found in the mineral gadolinite and other minerals together with other rare earths  For more information see the data from ChemGlobe '),
(95997, 'Thumb', 'The short thick first digit of the human hand differing from the other fingers in having but two phalanges the pollex See Pollex'),
