(97189, 'Traditor', 'A deliverer    a name of infamy given to Christians who delivered the Scriptures or the goods of the church to their persecutors to save their lives'),
(97190, 'Traduce', 'To transfer to transmit to hand down as to traduce mental qualities to ones descendants'),
