(104346, 'Victoria', 'A genus of aquatic plants named in honor of Queen Victoria  The Victoria regia is a native of Guiana and Brazil  Its large spreading leaves are often over five feet in diameter and have a rim from three to five inches high its immense rose white flowers sometimes attain a diameter of nearly two feet'),
