(104673, 'Vitamin', 'any of several organic chemical substances not synthesized by an animal and required in small quantities for normal metabolism present in and obtained from the natural foods eaten by the animal  Human vitamins are also produced synthetically and taken in pure form or in mixtures as dietary supplements  Deficiencies of specific vitamins lead to certain specific disorders such as scurvy caused by an insufficiency of vitamin C ascorbic acid'),
