(105198, 'Wall sided', 'Having sides nearly perpendicular    said of certain vessels to distinguish them from those having flaring sides or sides tumbling home see under Tumble v i'),
(105199, 'Wall Street', 'A street towards the southern end of the borough of Manhattan New York City extending from Broadway to the East River    so called from the old wall which extended along it when the city belonged to the Dutch It is the chief financial center of the United States hence the name is often used for the money market and the financial interests of the country    in American financial publications also referred to as the street'),
