(106302, 'Whitefish', 'Any one of several species of Coregonus a genus of excellent food fishes allied to the salmons They inhabit the lakes of the colder parts of North America Asia and Europe The largest and most important American species Coregonus clupeiformis is abundant in the Great Lakes and in other lakes farther north Called also lake whitefish and Oswego bass'),
(106303, 'Whiteflaw', 'A whitlow'),
(106304, 'White fly', 'Any one of numerous small injurious hemipterous insects of the genus Aleyrodes allied to scale insects They are usually covered with a white or gray powder'),
(106305, 'White foot', 'A white mark on the foot of a horse between the fetlock and the coffin'),
(106306, 'White friar', 'A mendicant monk of the Carmelite order so called from the white cloaks worn by the order  See Carmelite'),
(106307, 'White fronted', 'Having a white front as the white fronted lemur'),
