(106411, 'Why', 'A young heifer'),
(106412, 'Whydah bird', 'The whidah bird'),
(106413, 'Why not', 'A violent and peremptory procedure without any assigned reason a sudden conclusive happening'),
(106414, 'Wicca', 'A religion derived from pre Christian times also called Witchcraft4 which practices a benevolent reverence for nature and recognizes two deities variously viewed as Mother  Father Goddess  God Female  Male etc its practitioners are called Wiccans Wiccas or witches  Since there is no central authority to propagate dogma the beliefs and practices of Wiccans vary significantly'),
