(107187, 'X', 'X the twenty fourth letter of the English alphabet has three sounds a compound nonvocal sound that of ks as in wax a compound vocal sound that of gz as in example and at the beginning of a word a simple vocal sound that of z as in xanthic  See Guide to Pronunciation '),
(107188, 'Xanthamide', 'An amido derivative of xanthic acid obtained as a white crystalline substance C2H5OCSNH2    called also xanthogen amide'),
(107189, 'Xanthate', 'A salt of xanthic a xanthogenate'),
(107190, 'Xanthelasma', 'See Xanthoma'),
(107191, 'Xanthian', 'Of or pertaining to Xanthus an ancient town on Asia Minor    applied especially to certain marbles found near that place and now in the British Museum'),
(107192, 'Xanthide', 'A compound or derivative of xanthogen'),
(107193, 'Xanthidium', 'A genus of minute unicellular algae of the desmids These algae have a rounded shape and are armed with glochidiate or branched aculei Several species occur in ditches and others are found fossil in flint or hornstone'),
(107194, 'Xanthin', 'same as xanthine'),
(107195, 'Xanthine', 'A type of purine obtainable as a white microcrystalline powder C5H4O2N4 present in muscle tissue in the liver spleen pancreas and other organs and also in urine in small quantities and some urinary calculi and in the juices of certain plants    so called because it leaves a yellow residue when evaporated to dryness with nitric acid It is also present in guano  Xanthine is closely related to uric acid'),
(107196, 'Xanthinine', 'A complex nitrogenous substance related to urea and uric acid produced as a white powder    so called because it forms yellow salts and because its solution forms a blue fluorescence like quinine'),
(107197, 'Xanthium', 'A genus of composite plants in which the scales of the involucre are united so as to form a kind of bur cocklebur clotbur'),
(107198, 'Xantho ', 'A combining form from Gr xanqos yellow as in xanthocobaltic salts Used also adjectively in chemistry'),
(107199, 'Xanthocarpous', 'Having yellow fruit'),
(107200, 'Xanthochroi', 'A division of the Caucasian races comprising the lighter colored members'),
