(107354, 'Y', 'Y the twenty fifth letter of the English alphabet at the beginning of a word or syllable except when a prefix see Y  is usually a fricative vocal consonant as a prefix and usually in the middle or at the end of a syllable it is a vowel  See Guide to Pronunciation '),
