(107414, 'Yarrish', 'Having a rough dry taste'),
(107415, 'Yarrow', 'An American and European composite plant Achillea Millefolium with very finely dissected leaves and small white corymbed flowers It has a strong and somewhat aromatic odor and taste and is sometimes used in making beer or is dried for smoking Called also milfoil and nosebleed'),
